# Troia secrets — copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and fill real values.
# NEVER commit real secrets. The repo only ever contains these placeholders.
#
# Three separate Stellar keypairs (no collapse, even on testnet):
TROIA_ADMIN_SECRET=
TROIA_OPERATOR_SECRET=
TROIA_ISSUER_SECRET=
#
# iyzico (fiat leg) API credentials:
IYZICO_API_KEY=
IYZICO_SECRET_KEY=
#
# Webhook HMAC verification secret (iyzico signs the callback with the account secretKey unless a distinct key is
# issued; blank -> IYZICO_SECRET_KEY is used):
WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=
#
# The PUBLIC url iyzico redirects the customer's browser to after payment — a tunnel on testnet pointing at the
# /return landing page (e.g. cloudflared: the https URL + /return). REQUIRED by `just serve`. Settlement is driven
# by the poll worker's server-side pull, not this URL. See docs/LIVE_SMOKE.md.
TROIA_CALLBACK_URL=
#
# Optional server tunables (sane defaults if blank): PORT=3000, HOST=0.0.0.0, POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5000 (>=1000),
# TROIA_DEPLOYMENT_PATH=deployment.testnet.json. Bad values fail the boot CLOSED (never a silent degrade).
# PORT=
# POLL_INTERVAL_MS=
#
# Where the append-only accounting journal and settlement-evidence logs are kept (default ./data, git-ignored).
# These are what survive a restart: the ledger's expected pool balance and the set of payouts we authorized.
# The directory is created 0700 and its files 0600 — they carry signed envelopes and merchant destinations.
# TROIA_DATA_DIR=data
#
# How often the settlement worker arms money-good orders and refills the pool from their collected TRY. This is
# the cadence RECON_INTERVAL_MS below must stay above. Default 5000 (min 1000).
# SETTLEMENT_TICK_MS=5000
#
# The COMPRESSED settlement valör for the demo, in SECONDS — how long after an order is armed the pool refill
# fires. The real iyzico valör is ~21 days; the demo squeezes it so the refill is visible inside a short
# walkthrough. Default 30 (min 1).
# DEMO_VALOR_SECS=30
#
# How often the solvency tripwire weighs the on-chain pool balance against the ledger's expectation. Must exceed
# SETTLEMENT_TICK_MS: a payout lands on chain before the settlement worker books it, and reading inside that
# window would report bookkeeping in flight as drift. Default 30000.
#
# The minimum binds this default too: raise SETTLEMENT_TICK_MS above 29000 and leave this one blank, and the boot
# FAILS rather than quietly running the drift check too fast. Raise one, set the other.
# RECON_INTERVAL_MS=30000
#
# How often the payout tail asks the chain which transactions took USDC out of the pool, and whether each one was
# authorized by this operator. It is a read-only observer on a slower cadence than the money path. Default 20000.
# Note its window: Soroban RPC keeps contract events for a rolling period (~7 days), so a tail that is down longer
# than that has a gap it can never re-read. It says so loudly; the solvency drift alarm covers the gap.
# OUTFLOW_INTERVAL_MS=20000
#
# How often the live audit asks whether the chain agrees with our books, order by order. It finds each order's
# settlement by the identifier the CONTRACT indexes, not by the transaction hash we recorded — which is the only
# way a DIFFERENT transaction settling our order can ever be noticed. Must exceed OUTFLOW_INTERVAL_MS: an order
# cannot be reconciled before the tail has observed its settlement. Default 30000.
# RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS=30000
